{"jsonrpc":"2.0","t":15240,"method":"harness","params":{"epoch":"f941abb68d58","items":[{"anchor":{"bytes":15861,"epoch":"74035fd36193a0b8","line":20,"needle":"❯"},"assistant":{"partial":false,"text":"`POST /login` takes a JSON body with `email` and `password`.\n\n- **Bad input:** if either field is missing or not a string, it returns `400 {error: \"email and password are required\"}`.\n- **Bad credentials:** an unknown email or wrong password returns `401 {error: \"invalid credentials\"}`.\n- **Success:** it returns `200 {id, email}`.\n\nPassword check is in `src/users.ts`. It looks the user up by email, hashes the given password with `scrypt` and the user's salt, then compares hashes with `timingSafeEqual`.\n\nGaps right now:\n- No token, session, or cookie is issued. Success only echoes the user's id and email.\n- One hardcoded in-memory user: `user@example.com`, with a salt hardcoded in source.\n- Unknown email returns early without hashing, so response time leaks whether the email exists.\n- No rate limiting or lockout."},"at":"2026-11-08T13:07:22.244Z","id":"msg_011CgqWfArYFbkUehQenSAtA","kind":"assistant","seq":11,"turnId":"08a23f9a-20c1-47d0-9c28-21ca04b9a66e"}],"kind":"items","sessionId":"s_viqfwhqaoo","ts":"2026-11-08T08:07:22.424977-05:00"}}
